1
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:07,519
So people who are familiar with the hillside\h
hermitage teachings will likely have heard the\h\h

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:15,599
word 'context' used with reference to the practice.\h
So can we go over what exactly that context is\h\h

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:22,029
and is it something one finds already there\h
or is it something one needs to cultivate?

4
00:00:27,662 --> 00:00:32,079
The context is definitely not\h
something that you fabricate.

5
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:35,394
It's not an idea that...

6
00:00:37,393 --> 00:00:40,393
There is a\h
component of let's say intellectual reflection to it,

7
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:48,879
but it would be more accurate to see\h
it at the level of an emotional perspective\h\h

8
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:54,479
or an emotional attitude, rather than just an idea 
that you can kind of keep at the back of your mind.

9
00:00:54,480 --> 00:01:02,559
So in the most practical sense, you\hcould say 
the context refers to your present state of mind.\h\h

10
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:10,079
That is the context that underlies your\h
actions and that even if you ignore it, it's still there,\h\h

11
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:18,217
which is an important thing to understand.\h
It's not that you're doing the context necessarily\hconsciously,

12
00:01:18,218 --> 00:01:24,016
but you're certainly responsible\h
for cultivating the context by acting out of\hstates of

13
00:01:24,017 --> 00:01:28,639
let's say greed or aversion that might\hbe there. 
Even if you're not saying to yourself\h\h

14
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:34,079
"I shall act out of this context and cultivate\h
this context", through your actions coming out of\h\h

15
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:39,999
that state of mind, that is the context that you\h
are increasing and strengthening.\h

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,959
So that's why the suttas would say that somebody who...
they\hwould describe it as "giving attention\h\h

17
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:54,479
to the sign of gratification" or "the theme of\h
gratification" that when somebody does that,

18
00:01:54,480 --> 00:02:03,039
their sensual desire increases. So it's not necessarily\h
that you tell yourself "I shall cultivate\h\h

19
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:10,559
the context of sensuality being pleasant and\h
agreeable". Your mind has that context already\h\h

20
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:16,319
of finding pleasure in these things and then by\h
you acting out of it you make it worse.

21
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:23,520
You make it even more easy for your mind to focus on\h
the pleasant aspect of sensuality and overlook the danger.

22
00:02:25,005 --> 00:02:30,959
So there is a right context and a\h
wrong context. Exactly. So then in a way it's\h\h

23
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:37,039
useful to recognize that this is not a new... that\h
the development of the context is not a new thing.\h\h

24
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:41,759
It's something that you've already been doing\h
all the time. It's just more often than not the\h\h

25
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:48,479
wrong kind of context. So the context of, 
like\hI said, finding pleasure in sensuality,\h\h

26
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:54,879
resisting the unpleasant, that's another context\h
that's pretty much by default there. And then if\h\h

27
00:02:54,880 --> 00:03:01,599
you don't question it and you just go about\h
your day as an ordinary person, you will be\h\h

28
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:06,639
cultivating that context. And distraction is to\h
cultivate the context of ignorance. Exactly. Yes.\h\h

29
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:11,039
So that's another one that's... 
You\hdon't need to make any effort. It's going to be\h\h

30
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:16,639
there by itself just because that's the starting\h
point of an ignorant mind. So then if you don't\h\h

31
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:21,839
make an effort to... That's why it's so important to\h
question the motivation behind your actions which\h\h

32
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:29,119
doesn't, as we've often clarified, is not about\h
a reason that you can kind of explain at\h\h

33
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:36,799
arms length. It's at that emotional level, which\h
means you need to ask yourself, you need to\h\h

34
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:43,279
uncover the motivation that's already there.\h
Not like you choose the motivation;

35
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:51,119
rather if you look you will see there is some\h
kind of force that's driving you to do X or Y\h\h

36
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:56,079
and that's where you would be able to see: Oh\h
is there a context of wanting to, like you\h\h

37
00:03:56,080 --> 00:04:02,079
said, distraction; or wanting to turn away from\h
the neutral feeling of not much going on.

38
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:06,559
Well, that's a context that would be there enduring\h
on its own. And by overlooking it, you're\h

39
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:12,799
acting out of it and you're making it even more...\h
you're taking yourself even farther away from\h\h

40
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:18,159
the wholesome context of non-distraction. 
Or from\hrecognizing any context whatsoever.

41
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:24,159
Exactly. Yes, because that's the other problem with 
the context\hof the unwholesome ones; the context of\h\h

42
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:30,879
greed, aversion, and delusion; of sensuality,\h
ill will, cruelty. It's that they...\h

43
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:39,679
you can't mindfully cultivate that context. In other words,\h
you can't mindfully engage in sensuality,\h\h

44
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:44,479
mindfully engage in ill will, mindfully engage in\h
cruelty, mindfully engage in destruction. That's a\h\h

45
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:51,839
contradiction in terms. So you would\h
then realize that: Well, that's pretty much the\h\h

46
00:04:51,840 --> 00:05:01,919
primary harm of these things. Even if I don't\hsee 
an immediate harm from it yet,\h\h

47
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:07,119
the simple fact that it obstructs your\h
self-awareness means like it's pretty\h\h

48
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:13,199
much like taking an intoxicant. Like, you don't\h
know what you're going to end up doing if you\h\h

49
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:18,959
take enough of an intoxicating substance.\h
Well, it's the same thing. And actually\h\h

50
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:25,919
the Buddha called it intoxication, and
one of the translations for this term\h\h

51
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:33,519
that's often rendered as heedfulness is non-\h
intoxication,  appamāda, which is exactly what you\h\h

52
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:39,519
will be cultivating. You would realize your\h
normal context, your normal state of being,

53
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:45,839
is one of intoxication with one thing or the other.\h
It doesn't necessarily have to be full-on coarse\h

54
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:54,319
sensual pleasure. You're just intoxicated with\h– 
in the broadest sense – life as such; with\h\h

55
00:05:54,320 --> 00:06:00,799
your ambitions, your goals, the things that\h
you value. Your health, protecting your health\h\h

56
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:05,599
for its own sake, not even for the\h
sake of practice, but just because you resist\h\h

57
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:12,719
illness as such. Intoxication with youth, as if, 
you know, it were ultimately in your\hcontrol.

58
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:18,159
Yes. Or like: "I can do it because I'm\h
still young and even if it goes wrong, I have\h\h

59
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:25,199
time in the future to correct my mistakes", which\h
is all based on assumptions that are dangerous.\h\h

60
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:32,559
Yes. And also, even if you don't have\h
something that fits neatly in one of\h\h

61
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:37,999
those three categories, well ultimately you will be\h
intoxicated with some sight, sound, smell, taste,\h\h

62
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:45,439
touch or even mental image. So you might have even\h
ideas about the practice and they might be right ideas,

63
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:54,959
but you often see that how somebody\h
could become so engaged on that level\h\h

64
